    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 73.04 score represents our most efficient start. Facing the moderate arm of Pallante, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable right-handed platoon advantage that pads his base projection by 14%. Right alongside him, **Cole Carrigg** offers elite value (71.23) as a switch-hitter against Martinez; his capacity for stolen bases remains a priority for our strategy, and the 19% SP skill boost makes him an essential fixture in the two-hole. **Jacob Wilson** also secures a top-tier slot (68.83), as the matchup against Lowder provides the high-contact environment necessary to stabilize our 5x5 categories.\n\nWhile the core of our offense is locked in, we have had to navigate some difficult tactical decisions. **Jorge Polanco** was the toughest exclusion from the starting nine, falling just short at 53.68 due to a suboptimal #8 spot in the order and a neutral matchup against Bibee. We have also had to weigh significant environmental risks, specifically the 36% rain probability hanging over the **Coby Mayo** and **Gunnar Henderson** matchup against Detmers. Despite the weather, both players remain in the lineup due to their dynamic platoon potential and high base utility, though we will monitor the radar closely. **Drake Baldwin** faces a similar rain risk (33%) in his contest against P\u00e9rez, but his prime lead-off position keeps his efficiency score well above the marginal threshold.\n\nFinally, we are keeping a close watch on **Jackson Merrill**, whose lineup position remains pending. While our model assumes an #5 slot, the matchup against the weak arm of Bratt (6.59 xERA) gives **Jackson Merrill** immense upside, making him a \"must-start\" regardless of where he lands in the order. Conversely, **Luis Lara** was easily relegated to the bench today, as a brutal encounter with Skenes cratered his score to a 34.93, falling well below our 40-point floor for active play. As we navigate this heavy-hitter slate, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of **Nasim Nunez** and **Heliot Ramos** to secure the steals category while relying on the consistent power outputs from **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** to drive our run and RBI production.",
